.TH BENCHMAN 1 "March 2026" "InfoTheory" "InfoTheory Benchmark Tools"
.SH NAME
benchman \- interactive InfoTheory benchmark and log-loss TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B projman.sh tui
[\-\-suite NAME]
[\-\-summary\-tsv PATH]
[\-\-baseline\-summary\-tsv PATH]
[\-\-raw\-tsv PATH]
[\-\-subjects LIST]
[\-\-plot\-dir PATH]
.PP
.B projman.sh tui log\-loss
.I PREFIX
.PP
.B projman.sh tui man
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B benchman
is a keyboard-only scientific analysis helper for InfoTheory TSV outputs.
It provides two modes:
.IP \(bu 2
benchmark inspection for all graph families produced by
.B scripts/plot_two_json.sh
including current-vs-baseline overlays
.IP \(bu
AC log-loss inspection for
.B infotheory ac\-log\-loss
diagnostic prefixes containing
.I .trace.tsv
,
.I .nodes.tsv
,
and
.I .summary.tsv
.PP
Both modes preserve the same overall interaction style: vi-like keyboard
navigation, graph switching, focused inspection, and exact value readout.
.PP
Benchmark mode supports:
.IP \(bu 2
graph navigation across all benchmark plot families
.IP \(bu
series focus/filtering for subject comparisons
.IP \(bu
cursor-based point inspection with exact x/y values
.IP \(bu
overlap detection when multiple visible series share the same point
.IP \(bu
optional raw TSV enrichment for per-repetition details
.PP
Log-loss mode supports:
.IP \(bu 2
mixture/oracle/regret/entropy/margin graphs over file position
.IP \(bu
domain partition views based on oracle-best expert with adjustable uncovered and contested thresholds
.IP \(bu
blind-spot and ensemble-advantage views
.IP \(bu
region inspection with exact byte previews, worst positions, and per-node statistics
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Benchmark Mode
.TP
.B \-\-suite NAME
Benchmark suite name (
.B two\-json
or
.B extra
). Controls latest-summary discovery and plot regeneration context.
.TP
.B \-\-summary\-tsv PATH
Summary TSV (defaults to newest
.I /tmp/infotheory-<suite>-summary-*.tsv
).
.TP
.B \-\-baseline\-summary\-tsv PATH
Optional baseline summary TSV for overlay graphs.
.TP
.B \-\-raw\-tsv PATH
Optional raw TSV for per-repetition inspector details.
.TP
.B \-\-subjects LIST
Comma/whitespace separated subject filter.
.TP
.B \-\-plot\-dir PATH
Artifact directory (default:
.I /tmp/plotimgs
).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-replot
Do not run plot regeneration script when rebuilding the plot directory.
.SS Log-Loss Mode
.TP
.I PREFIX
Path prefix for
.I PREFIX.trace.tsv
,
.I PREFIX.nodes.tsv
,
and
.I PREFIX.summary.tsv
produced by
.B infotheory ac\-log\-loss
.
.SH KEYBOARD
.SS Shared Navigation
.TP
.B h/l
or
.B Left/Right
Move cursor across x points.
.TP
.B j/k
or
.B Down/Up
Move cursor across visible series.
.TP
.B [ ]
Previous / next graph.
.TP
.B g / G
First / last graph.
.TP
.B f
Open series focus/filter popup.
.TP
.B Enter
Inspect exact values at current cursor x for all visible lines.
.TP
.B c
or
.B Esc
Clear inspector popup.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SS Log-Loss Mode Extras
.TP
.B z / Z / a
Zoom into the current region, zoom out, or reset to the full file.
.TP
.B b / B
Decrease / increase the uncovered-oracle threshold.
.TP
.B m / M
Decrease / increase the contested-margin threshold.
.TP
.B r / R
Decrease / increase the blind-spot regret threshold.
.TP
.B w / W
Decrease / increase the blind-spot good-expert threshold.
.TP
.B ?
Open log-loss help with the exact partitioning rule and threshold controls.
.SH PLOT ARTIFACT DIRECTORY
When the plot directory already exists, benchman prompts:
.IP "A" 4
Use current artifacts (assume up-to-date).
.IP "B" 4
Remove and regenerate via
.B scripts/plot_two_json.sh
.
.SH MANUAL VIEW
Use:
.PP
.B projman.sh tui man
.PP
This sets:
.PP
.B MANPAGER='nvim +Man!'
.PP
and opens this local manual through
.BR man (1)
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.SS Benchmark Mode
.TP
.B INFOTHEORY_PLOT_SUMMARY_TSV
Summary TSV path.
.TP
.B INFOTHEORY_PLOT_SUITE
Benchmark suite (
.B two\-json
or
.B extra
).
.TP
.B INFOTHEORY_BASELINE_SUMMARY_TSV
Baseline summary TSV path.
.TP
.B INFOTHEORY_BENCH_RAW_TSV
Raw TSV path.
.TP
.B INFOTHEORY_PLOT_SUBJECTS
Subject filter list.
.TP
.B INFOTHEORY_PLOT_OUTPUT_DIR
Plot artifact directory.
.SS Log-Loss Mode
Log-loss mode reads the diagnostic files directly from the supplied
.I PREFIX
and does not require additional environment variables.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR projman.sh (1),
.BR scripts/bench_two_json.sh (1),
.BR scripts/plot_two_json.sh (1),
.BR infotheory (1)
